Proxmox: DR Replica VM Migration Guide
This procedure outlines the safe steps for migrating a Disaster Recovery (DR) replica virtual machine from a source server to a target server in Proxmox.

Step 1: Replication Status Pre-Check
Before initiating the migration, verify that no active replication process will conflict with the operation:

Go to the Notes of the original source VM.

Check the replication variable value: repActive = on / off.

If it is off (meaning replication is not currently running), it is safe to proceed.

On the original VM, update the note from rep=on to rep=off.

Step 2: Migration Command
You can run the following dynamic migration command (replace XXX with the vmID and YYY with the target host identifier):

Bash
vmID=XXX
kvTargetNip=kvYYY-45-83-41-141
targetStorage=$(echo ${kvTargetNip} | cut -d'-' -f1)_storage1

qm migrate ${vmID} ${kvTargetNip} --targetstorage ${targetStorage} && printf '\a'

Step 3: Fallback Offline Migration Command
If the dynamic command does not work or fails, you can use a direct offline migration command (example shown with specific IDs):

Bash
qm migrate 1577 kv0228-194-146-38-98 --targetstorage kv0228_storage1
